LRC14 pair-good decoy classifier
threshold=1/14

Definition: a pair-good decoy is a THM-524 candidate time where at least one
pair has equal distance >= 1/14, but the full row has min_v ||v t|| < 1/14.
The classifier records the exact pair lane and the blocker deck, so decoys
are generated by switch classes rather than counted as anonymous threats.

