[BARCODE / NORMAL-FAN RELATION]
  Pair-good decoys are outside strict barcode bars by definition: actual_gap < 1/14.
  Their proof role is controlled by whether the good pair or the blocker deck
  reappears as a true normal-fan peak support.  In the named audit the common
  cases are pair-overlap or blocker-overlap with real supports; the remaining
  disjoint classes are generated by explicit denominator lanes and blocker decks.
  Therefore decoy counts are not proof obligations once the generator grammar is kept.

[TOURNAMENT ANALYSIS]
vertices=proof carriers / decoy-generator grammars, not runners
observable=(predicate, generator_exactness, blocker_deck, barcode_relation, normal_fan_relation, family_routing, anti_counting_value)
switch=majority comparison; tie path=listed carrier order
score_hist={0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 4: 1, 5: 1, 6: 1}
directed_3cycles=0
scc_sizes=[1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1]
hamiltonian_path_count=1
score_order=pair_good_generator_grammar > active_bottleneck_normal_fan > binding_pair_switch_with_clearance > lonely_profile_persistence_barcode > automaton_fiber_magnitude_cocycle > raw_pair_gap_count > raw_pair_good_boolean
  pair_good_generator_grammar: score=6 vector=(3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3) note=classifies pair-good times by exact lane, shell, and blockers
  active_bottleneck_normal_fan: score=5 vector=(3, 2, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3) note=links decoys to true bar supports and endpoint owners
  binding_pair_switch_with_clearance: score=4 vector=(3, 3, 2, 2, 2, 3, 3) note=keeps THM-524 support plus clearance scan
  lonely_profile_persistence_barcode: score=3 vector=(3, 1, 1, 3, 3, 2, 3) note=knows strict bars but not blocked pair generators
  automaton_fiber_magnitude_cocycle: score=2 vector=(2, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 3) note=repairs mixed automaton fibers but not pair decoys
  raw_pair_gap_count: score=1 vector=(1, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1) note=counts decoys without explaining their generation
  raw_pair_good_boolean: score=0 vector=(0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0) note=forgets blockers and creates false threats
